Ladybird now hangs an ideographic space at the end of a line under
white-space normal, nowrap, and pre-line, and keeps the other space
separators on the line. Run in Chrome 157, a trailing U+3000 neither
made a full line wrap nor moved right-aligned or centered text, and
Chrome kept an em space on the line, as Ladybird now does. Firefox 151
hangs the ideographic space only where it overflows the line, and WebKit
26.5 never hangs it. That comparison comes from running the engines;
their code for it wasn’t traced.
